## Current implication chain

For strict packets at the ORIGINAL canonical source:

    one protected spare site after replacing all old interior labels
    -> delete any nonisolated vertex and strictly refill
    -> same cardinality, triangle-free, diameter <= D, fewer contacts
    -> contradict canonical contact minimality or global optimality.

Thus s_Z=o(D) versus s_Z=Omega(D) does not alter the integer capacity target
for this endpoint. Paying kappa<=s_Z+1 is sufficient for a strict sub-D
construction, but is stronger than necessary when a strict packet exists
before motion. This observation does not prove packet existence.

For packets available only AFTER motion:

    delete a positive KKT-support transversal
    -> strict opening/diameter descent on the reduced source
    -> a controlled finite continuation reaching actual capacity
    -> restore every deleted label by a certified strict packet.

Only the first strict step is proved. Finite continuation and cardinality
recovery are unresolved.

