## Periodic-packing source check: no imported capacity theorem

Checked Connelly--Dickinson, *Periodic Planar Disk Packings*, author PDF
https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~connelly/Connelly-Dickinson-V3.pdf
(pp. 5--8, 15--17; also arXiv:1201.5965). The general one-disk density
gap is explicitly Conjectures 2--3, not a proved theorem. Theorem 9
classifies collectively jammed all-rhombus packings on a fixed torus:
congruent two-direction rhombi and tours visiting every vertex. Theorem 4's
density result requires a triangular torus, only triangle/rhombus faces,
and its stated vertex-degree hypotheses. Canonical Target C's physical
exceptional faces and finite loaded boundary supply neither a torus
co-embedding nor those face hypotheses. Thus this literature does not
prove strict refill for the unit loaded-hull cycle or terminate the finite
pivot route. No density gap or periodic boundary identification is
imported. Eppstein's original 2018 paper, Figure 2 and Lemma 1, also
explicitly permits all convex-hull vertices to have degree three; its
low-degree vertices need not be hull vertices. It supplies no stronger
convex-wall packing-capacity theorem here.

