## Loaded-neighbor incidence and outer-owner capacity

Canonical diameter midpoint concentration makes every bounded loaded
cluster an almost straight hull chain. Three loaded neighbors in a fixed
source annulus [1,t], t<sqrt(2), would converge to three separated collinear
points in that annulus, which is impossible. Thus every source vertex
has at most two such loaded neighbors. Near-unit loaded-loaded pairs are
consecutive full-hull pairs; noncontacts charge nonunit loaded-hull sides.
Combining these with audit.61's actual outer-face singleton witnesses
gives k<=2m_B+3(x_B+Z_out), replacing the older q-sized boundary capacity.
A linear safe owner family with sublinear hull/outer defects therefore
forces linear outer isolates. Actual O--O extraction, unary safety,
upper-exception handling and the isolate bank remain explicit unresolved
hypotheses; pentagon-pair trains are not silently relabeled O--O proposals.

